# Code owners for Holotable.
#
# Listed paths require a review from the owner before merge. The point is not
# process for its own sake: these are the files where a quiet regression stops
# being a bug and starts being a vulnerability. See SECURITY.md and
# docs/src/content/docs/architecture/invariants.md.

# Default owner for anything not matched below.
*                               @jbouder

# The SQL guard. Everything the model emits passes through here: SELECT-only,
# catalog allowlist, denylist, row and time limits, read-only execution.
/src/lib/sql/                   @jbouder

# Authentication and authorization. OIDC session handling, claim parsing
# (highest role wins, fail-closed), and the central can() check.
/src/lib/auth/                  @jbouder

# The shared IR — the contract between model output, API validation,
# persistence, and the client. A change here changes all four.
/src/lib/ir.ts                  @jbouder

# Server-side time resolution and range injection. The server, not the client
# or the model, decides what window a panel actually queries.
/src/lib/time.ts                @jbouder

# The source registry: safe connection config, catalog, and secret_ref
# resolution. Credentials come from the environment here and are never stored.
/src/lib/registry.ts            @jbouder

# The /api/metrics gate. A scrape names dashboards and sources, per-workspace
# model spend, and what the SQL guard is rejecting, and it sits outside the
# session cookie — so loosening this file is a disclosure, not a config change.
/src/lib/metrics-access.ts      @jbouder

# Security policy, contributor expectations, and the license.
/SECURITY.md                    @jbouder
/CONTRIBUTING.md                @jbouder
/LICENSE                        @jbouder
/NOTICE                         @jbouder

# CI and repository automation.
/.github/                       @jbouder
